or": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01UGQfsip7xTrDzZitokAq8t", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-08d3cd5986", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 379781, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01UGQfsip7xTrDzZitokAq8t", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 383960, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `src/money.py`'s docstring said it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, per FIN-212), but the code actually used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. That's why `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` failed: it expects 2.665 to round down to 2.66.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, I changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on commit `08d3cd5986`.\n- **PR:** #101 is at https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101.\n\nI tried to look up FIN-212 with the advisory lookup tool, but it doesn't know that ID. It's probably an internal ticket, not a security advisory, so I relied on the docstring and the test for the expected behaviour.\n\nI haven't merged the PR. Merging into main needs code-owner approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_015YZqbf5EWtXWUVeyxApysb", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01EaGwed5ZpZkME8G1wydCf5", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01RMAianUKwEH6qH4zicXcY7", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type"