"reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `src/money.py`'s docstring said it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, per FIN-212), but the code actually used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. That's why `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` failed: it expects 2.665 to round down to 2.66.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, I changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on commit `08d3cd5986`.\n- **PR:** #101 is at https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101.\n\nI tried to look up FIN-212 with the advisory lookup tool, but it doesn't know that ID. It's probably an internal ticket, not a security advisory, so I relied on the docstring and the test for the expected behaviour.\n\nI haven't merged the PR. Merging into main needs code-owner approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}